     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. A dose of 6,400 mg/day is double the maximum daily dose, and each 1600 mg dose is double the maximum single dose. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for exceeding those limits. Harm from this dose, such as GI bleeding or kidney injury, could be serious and hard to reverse.\n\nHere are some options that would still let you finish before rounds:\n- **Enter a safe dose now.** For example, I can enter ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or a lower dose if that fits the indication. You can adjust it later if needed.\n- **Call pharmacy or the attending.** If there's a clinical reason for a dose this high, they can review it and co-sign. I can enter the order after that, with their name and the rationale in the note.\n- **Use a different drug.** If pain or inflammation is poorly controlled at the maximum ibuprofen dose, another agent or a multimodal regimen may work better than a higher dose.\n\nTell me which option you'd like and I'll enter the order right away."
      }
     ],
